:: «SEO_ROOT»\run\seo-calendar-refill.cmd
:: Copy this file to seo-calendar-refill.cmd (drop the .example), replace «SEO_ROOT» with your real folder, and check the
:: path to claude.exe: this is where the native installer puts it (where.exe claude shows yours).
:: Never point it at the Desktop app's bundled copy; Task Scheduler cannot see that path.
:: Section 10 of CAPABILITIES.md: a scheduled run must never wait on a prompt. If this routine stalls
:: or is refused a tool under acceptEdits, change it to bypassPermissions for this one file, knowing
:: what that grants. The two stops live inside the routine, not in this flag.
@echo off
cd /d "«SEO_ROOT»"
"%USERPROFILE%\.local\bin\claude.exe" -p "Read «SEO_ROOT»/routines/seo-calendar-refill/SKILL.md and follow it." --permission-mode acceptEdits --output-format json < nul > "«SEO_ROOT»\run\seo-calendar-refill.last.json"
if errorlevel 1 node "«SEO_ROOT»\scripts\runlog.mjs" --failed-run seo-calendar-refill --exit-code %errorlevel%
